WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.109
On a personal level.

2
00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:12.680
One example of a threat and its impact is unauthorized charges on your credit card.

3
00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:15.350
It's a good idea not to store your credit

4
00:00:15.359 --> 00:00:17.709
information in your phone or on your web browser.

5
00:00:17.719 --> 00:00:20.190
Even though that is convenient for online shopping,

6
00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:23.790
most banks won't charge you for unauthorized purchases,

7
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.620
but it may result in your account being frozen when you are trying to use it

8
00:00:27.879 --> 00:00:31.040
or the hassle of replacing a card that has been compromised and

9
00:00:31.049 --> 00:00:34.750
updating any subscriptions or bills that were paid directly with that card.

10
00:00:35.529 --> 00:00:37.950
If you identify a risk beforehand,

11
00:00:37.959 --> 00:00:39.659
you can mitigate it by adding layers

12
00:00:39.669 --> 00:00:42.560
of security such as multi factor authorization.

13
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.369
Most bank websites either require or at least encourage you to

14
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.590
set up multi factor authentication when you access your account.

15
00:00:49.889 --> 00:00:52.889
So you need a user name and password and also

16
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.549
a code sent to your email or your cell phone.

17
00:00:57.689 --> 00:01:01.159
Another example of handling risk is when you book a vacation.

18
00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:02.490
For example,

19
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.349
you might be considering a Caribbean cruise where the weather

20
00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.029
can be a factor and your trip could be canceled.

21
00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:11.989
In that case you purchase travel insurance to transfer the risk.

22
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.190
So you don't lose out on your prepaid expenses

23
00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:17.099
and deposits if something happens to prevent the trip,

24
00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:21.750
other types of insurance are also ways to transfer risk.

25
00:01:22.029 --> 00:01:25.300
You might purchase additional health care coverage to cover your expenses.

26
00:01:25.309 --> 00:01:26.410
If you have an accident.

27
00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:28.959
If you are concerned about identity theft,

28
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:32.690
there are companies that offer an insurance policy for managing your identity.

29
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:37.029
These companies are also involved in their own form of financial risk management.

30
00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.290
Calculating that your premium payments or

31
00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.769
subscription payments will exceed the payouts.

32
00:01:41.779 --> 00:01:44.010
They will have to make in the event of a claim.